A **regular 100-gon** is a polygon with 100 sides, all of equal length, and all internal angles equal. Because it is regular, it possesses **rotational symmetry** of order 100 (i.e., it looks identical after a rotation of $ \frac{360^\circ}{100} = 3.6^\circ $), and **reflection symmetry** across multiple axes through vertices and midpoints of edges.

